SUMMARY:On The Sea @ Merlin St Ives
DESCRIPTION:On The Sea (1h 55min)\nDrama\, Romance\n\nJack has been married
  to Maggie for over half his life. He works as a Hand Raker on the mussel 
 beds in North Wales alongside his younger brother\, Dyfan\, and Dyfan’s th
 ree sons. Jack has always assumed that his own boy\, Tom\, will join the f
 amily business on leaving school but Tom’s resistance to follow in his foo
 tsteps creates familial tension. Tensions are further inflamed by the arri
 val of an itinerant deckhand\, Daniel\, who makes known his feelings for J
 ack. In this remote\, rural community where life revolves around Church an
 d fishery\, Jack is faced with an impossible dilemma. On The Sea is a beau
 tiful\, sensual and at times\, tragic exploration of masculinity\, place a
 nd desire.\n\nStarring: Barry Ward\, Lorne MacFadyen\, Liz White\, Henry L
 awfull\, Celyn Jones\, Leisa Gwenllian\n\nFilm release at Merlin Cinemas S
 t Ives\nBook tickets: /film/on-the-sea\n\nFilm details: https://evenwebb.g
 ithub.io/merlin-cinemas/films/on-the-sea.html
LOCATION:Merlin Cinemas St Ives
URL:/film/on-the-sea
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
